            </Main>
            <WaterConservation LowFlushToilets="3" LowFlushToiletsUpgrade="0" />
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>During our visit the owner shared is concerns about a room builted over the garage and partially inside the roof. Some signs of condensation on the walls and specially on the corner were visible. The infiltration test shows some air leakage on this particular spots, which explain the condensation. Because the room was finished it was impossible to verify the level of insulation inside the wall, nor either to confirm the presence of insulation whithin the wall or the attic insulation.



Some spots are damged and therfore we recommend to open the walls in order to verify the composition of it and then re-insulate the section completly. The details for such king of jobs will be more than important to ensure that the wall envelope is air tight and sealed properly. The test shows us also other places in the house were there is some air laekage. But the must serious one is the room located on the upper floor above the garage.



</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>During the infiltration test we notice a lot of air coming from the corners of the room above garage and also signs of condensation. We recommend the insulation of the walls to reach a level of R-40. Once insulated make sure that the joints of the vapour barrier are well sealed and continous. We recommend also the replacement of the drywall.</mainWalls>
                <ceilingsCathedral>No acces to the roof, it is then difficult to verify the level of insulation. According to the age of the building and the heel height we estimate the insulation to be R-40. We recommend the addition of more insulation to meet the actual standard of R-60 or even R-70.



</ceilingsCathedral>
                <exposedFloors>We recommend the insulation of the floor of the room above garage. We suggest to put a level of insulation of R-30.</exposedFloors>
                <windows>The windows seems to be in good condition exept the ones locates in the master bedroom on the upper floor. The small windows are the originals pretty leaky. We recommend the replacement of these units by ENERGY STAR certified windows and suitable for ZONE 3.</windows>
                <doors>We recommend the replacement of the doors, specially the right door ( the old garage door). The weather strips are broken, we were able to see outside when the door was  closed. Also the back door are leaky, the air passes through the handles.



We recommend the replacement by ENERGY STAR certified units.</doors>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
